### MEDIUM: gemini (gemini-code-assist[bot])
**File**: `tests/unit/purchase.test.ts:44`
![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

While the schema test verifies that the `DELETED` status is allowed in the input, it would be beneficial to also include a functional test to ensure that this status is correctly passed to the QuickFile API in the `Purchase_Search` request. This confirms that the handler logic correctly processes the new enum value and maps it to the expected API parameter.

```typescript
    it("allows searching soft-deleted purchases by status", () => {
      const tool = purchaseTools.find(
        (candidate) => candidate.name === "quickfile_purchase_search",
      );

      expect(tool?.inputSchema).toMatchObject({
        properties: {
          status: {
            enum: ["UNPAID", "PAID", "PART_PAID", "CANCELLED", "DELETED"],
          },
        },
      });
    });

    it("passes the DELETED status to the API", async () => {
      mockRequest.mockResolvedValueOnce({ Record: [], RecordsetCount: 0 });

      await handlePurchaseTool("quickfile_purchase_search", {
        status: "DELETED",
      });

      expect(mockRequest).toHaveBeenCalledWith("Purchase_Search", {
        SearchParameters: {
          ReturnCount: 25,
          Offset: 0,
          OrderResultsBy: "ReceiptDate",
          OrderDirection: "DESC",
          Status: "DELETED",
        },
      });
    });
```

